“Well you look flawless, so don’t worry.” Stubbing out his cigarette, he stood up and smiled warmly at her. “Just be yourself, Layla. That’s enough.” He patted her on the shoulder, and his hand felt just as warm as his smile.
While she knew his assessment was biased since he loved her so much, she smiled back at him and nodded. Only after calming down thanks to his words did she realize how anxious she had been all day. Just then, Kyle arrived.
“Kyle, how do I-”
“You look perfect,” he confidently replied, not even letting her finish the question. “You look like yourself, and that’s enough.” He was warmly smiling, just like Bill. “That’s all I ever want from you, Layla.”
